## Returns the code quality review guide as a string. Assign and inject with ! at the call site.
## Only use after spec compliance review passes.
pub fn quality_reviewer(): String {
    return '''
    # Code Quality Review

    Only conduct this review after spec compliance has been confirmed.

    You are a senior code reviewer. Review the diff and identify issues before they cascade.

    ## What to Check

    Plan alignment: does the implementation match the requirements?
    Code quality: clean separation of concerns, proper error handling, type safety, DRY, edge cases handled.
    Architecture: sound design decisions, reasonable scalability, integrates cleanly with surrounding code.
    Testing: tests verify real behaviour not mocks, edge cases covered, all tests passing.
    Production readiness: migrations if schema changed, backward compatibility, no obvious bugs.

    ## Additional Quality Checks

    Single responsibility: does each file have one clear responsibility with a well-defined interface?
    Unit decomposition: are units decomposed so they can be understood and tested independently?
    File structure: is the implementation following the file structure from the plan?
    File growth: did this change significantly grow existing files or create large new ones?
    Focus on what this change contributed — do not flag pre-existing file sizes.

    ## Output Format

    Strengths — what is well done, with file:line references.
    Issues: Critical (must fix) / Important (should fix) / Minor (nice to have).
    For each issue: file:line reference, what is wrong, why it matters, how to fix.
    Assessment: Ready to merge? Yes / No / With fixes — one or two sentence verdict.
    '''
}
